.SH OPTIONS
\f[B]\-\-batch\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Specify a batch of commands to execute.
.TP
Example:
\f[B]hyprctl\f[R] \f[I]\-\-batch \(dqkeyword general:border_size 2 ;
keyword general:gaps_out 20\(dq\f[R]
.RS
.PP
\f[I];\f[R] separates the commands.
.RE
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\-j\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Outputs information in JSON.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\-\-plain\f[R]
.RS
.PP
(hyperctl) Print the plain upstream output, never the pretty one.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]\-\-pretty\f[R]
.RS
.PP
(hyperctl) Pretty\-print even when standard output is not a terminal.
.RE
.SH HYPERCTL
Invoked as \f[B]hyperctl\f[R] with standard output on a terminal,
replies are rendered as tables and cards by \f[B]hyperctl\-tui\f[R].
Invoked as \f[B]hyprctl\f[R], piped, or with \f[I]\-j\f[R],
\f[I]\-q\f[R] or \f[I]\-\-batch\f[R], the output is exactly that of
Hyprland\(aqs hyprctl.
When \f[B]hyperctl\-tui\f[R] is not installed the plain output is
printed.
.PP
\f[B]hyperctl tui\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Opens the interactive hyperctl\-tui interface.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\f[B]HYPERCTL_PRETTY\f[R]
.RS
.PP
\f[I]auto\f[R] (default), \f[I]always\f[R] or \f[I]never\f[R].
.RE
.PP
\f[B]HYPERCTL_RAW\f[R]
.RS
.PP
When set, hyperctl prints the plain output.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]NO_COLOR\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Disables colors in the pretty output.
.RE
